person/abu-shajara-amr-ibn-abd-al-uzza | A Sulami, son of al-Khansa'; he led a gathering of Banu Sulaym at Jaw Quraqir (some say al-Nuqra) and fought Khalid ibn al-Walid in the Ridda until God scattered their gathering after one Muslim fell a martyr; he later embraced Islam and came to Umar ibn al-Khattab as he was giving to the poor, begging of him — Umar said 'are you not the one who said: I have healed my spirit from Khalid's squadron, yet I hope to live long after it?' and struck him with the durra, to which he answered 'Islam has erased that, commander of the faithful'.
